 ### 6.1 Communications & Activity Stream
 
 **Communications** is the internal activity log used polymorphically across all ops modules. A sales agent logs a phone call against a lead; an HR admin logs a 1-on-1 against a person; a marketing manager logs a meeting against a campaign; a field agent logs a canvassing call against a project task — all in one `CommunicationsLog` table keyed by `(relatedEntityType, relatedEntityId)`. Includes follow-up reminders with assignment.
 
 **Threaded replies (P3, 2026-05-30).** Any message can be replied to (`parentId` self-FK, `onDelete: Cascade`). `CommunicationsService.findAll` returns only top-level messages (`where.parentId = null`) with their `replies` nested (ordered asc) — keep that `parentId: null` filter or replies also surface as duplicate top-level entries everywhere the timeline is embedded. Replies collapse to ONE level: a reply-to-a-reply re-parents onto the root (`parent.parentId ?? parent.id`) and inherits the parent's `relatedEntityType/Id`. Posting a reply pings the parent author in addition to the entity parties. UI: `CommunicationsTimeline.tsx` renders nested replies + an inline composer (`parentId` on the create payload); its action buttons (Log / Reply / Resolve / Delete) are `<Can>`-gated (`communications` CREATE/EDIT/DELETE) so a VIEW-only role gets a clean read-only timeline.
 
